    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0264" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.51/1015</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Chief of the Division
                        of the American Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bonsal</hi>)<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d286-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-15">June 15, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Costa Rican Minister came in to see me this morning. The Finance Minister,
                    Señor Escalante, still feels that the nine-year credit which we offered is not
                    wholly satisfactory. However, he has asked Francisco Calderón Guardia,<anchor
                        n="34" xml:id="d286-f2"/> who is in this country and who will be in
                    Washington on Wednesday and Thursday<anchor n="35" xml:id="d286-f3"/> to find
                    out whether we could not increase the amount to $2,000,000, leaving the terms
                    the same. The reason for this is that the taxes which it is proposed to encumber
                    for this purpose (probably the tobacco and beer taxes) produce 2,000,000 colones
                    per annum and would, therefore, warrant a larger credit than the $1,000,000
                    originally suggested. In other words, if these taxes are to be encumbered, the
                    Costa Ricans want to get the maximum credit.</p>
                <p>Please let me have an indication of your views as to the reply which we should
                    make.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi> W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Bonsal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d286-f1" n="33" type="source" xml:id="d286-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to Sumner Welles, Under Secretary of State, Laurence Duggan, Political
                    Adviser, and Emilio G. Collado, Special Assistant to Under Secretary Welles.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d286-f2" n="34" xml:id="d286-f2-content">
                <p>Costa Rican Minister of Interior and Public Security.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d286-f3" n="35" xml:id="d286-f3-content">
                <p>June 17 and 18.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
